Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||10-10-2000||06:32 PM||||A man walks into a bar. As he walks to the bar he notices a really small man playing the piano. He sits down and asks the bartender what the jar full of twenties was for, the bartender said that was a wishing jar. As the bartender walks away the man tosses in a 20 and wishes for a million bucks. Just then a million ducks come falling down from the sky. The bartender walks over and asks what he wished for. The man replied, "I wished for a million bucks!" Oh, said the bartender, I forgot to tell you to speak clearly, you think I wished for a 12" pianist?<p>[This message has been edited by SCCA FIERO (edited 10-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||wkayl||10-10-2000||08:36 PM||||A guy walks into a bar.  He places a head on the bar.  The bartender asks "what's the deal with this head?"  The guy says that 21 years ago today his son was born.  All that there was was just the head.  I'm taking him out for his birthday so give me a beer for him.  He tilts the head back, pores in the beer, and POOF!  A body pops out.  He gives him another beer and POOF!  Legs pop out.  He gives him another beer and POOF!  Arms pop out.  Great, now I have a complete son.  Give us another so we can celebrate.  The son drinks the beer and POOF!!!!  He disappears. <P>Moral of the story;<BR>Quit while you’re ahead…<BR>||||reg||1
